    "body": "## Summary\n- add authenticated `GET /jobs/recommended` with paginated newest-first recommendations\n- derive matching categories from the caller's active concrete service specializations\n- exclude the caller's own jobs and bilateral user-block relationships in the database query before pagination\n- return `specializationCount` so clients can distinguish profile setup from a genuine no-matches state\n- centralize public `Job -> JobResponse` mapping so recommendations and normal discovery share the same privacy-safe contract\n- add a `Dla Ciebie` recommendation section above normal discovery for signed-in users\n- hydrate bookmark state through the existing batch endpoint and keep duplicate cards synchronized with ordinary discovery\n- add unit coverage and focused recommendation/privacy documentation\n\n## Matching / privacy\n- only `OPEN` jobs whose leaf category exactly matches one of the caller's active specializations are recommended\n- `publicLocation` is not parsed or geocoded; this slice does not infer a worker location\n- recommendations expose only the normal public `JobResponse` fields; exact coordinates, participant-only addresses, routes, tracking, chat, wallet/payment/escrow and private verification/moderation data remain excluded\n- no job is accepted automatically and specialization selection does not imply availability\n\n## Schema\nNo new Flyway migration is required. The query reuses V33 `user_service_categories`, existing category/job indexes and block-aware discovery relationships.\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend dependency audit/lint/build and the full containers/runtime smoke. Do not merge unless the latest head is fully green.",
